WEBVTT

1
00:00:25.791 --> 00:00:30.041


2
00:00:30.041 --> 00:00:34.708
<b>After describing the infinite,</b>
<b>indestructible nature of the soul,</b>

3
00:00:34.708 --> 00:00:39.916
<b>here Lord Krishna explains to</b>
<b>Arjun in yet another way.</b>

4
00:00:39.916 --> 00:00:41.458
<b>He says,</b>

5
00:00:41.458 --> 00:00:43.166
<b>O Mighty-armed one,</b>

6
00:00:43.166 --> 00:00:49.833
<b>even if you believe that the soul is bound by</b>
<b>the laws of birth and death,</b>

7
00:00:49.833 --> 00:00:53.833
<b>still this is not worthy of your grief.</b>

8
00:00:54.500 --> 00:00:58.708


9
00:00:58.708 --> 00:01:00.125
<b>Mighty-armed one,</b>

10
00:01:00.125 --> 00:01:04.875
<b>meaning one whose arms possess</b>
<b>great strength.</b>

11
00:01:04.875 --> 00:01:10.625
<b>By addressing him thus, Krishna is reminding</b>
<b>Arjun again of his power.</b>

12
00:01:10.625 --> 00:01:11.541
<b>Moreover,</b>

13
00:01:11.541 --> 00:01:12.500
<b>He says,</b>

14
00:01:12.500 --> 00:01:17.083
<b>even if you consider the soul bound</b>
<b>by birth and death,</b>

15
00:01:17.083 --> 00:01:20.541
<b>still this is not a matter worthy of grief.</b>

16
00:01:20.541 --> 00:01:22.250
<b>Understand it this way</b>

17
00:01:22.250 --> 00:01:28.291
<b>if for argument's sake we accept that</b>
<b>the soul is bound by birth and death,</b>

18
00:01:28.291 --> 00:01:29.000
<b>then?</b>

19
00:01:29.000 --> 00:01:34.250
<b>Then wouldn't this mean that man is merely</b>
<b>a product of physical elements,</b>

20
00:01:34.250 --> 00:01:38.166
<b>just an existence perhaps made of earth,</b>

21
00:01:38.166 --> 00:01:39.000
<b>water,</b>

22
00:01:39.000 --> 00:01:39.958
<b>air,</b>

23
00:01:39.958 --> 00:01:41.166
<b>fire?</b>

24
00:01:41.166 --> 00:01:42.208
<b>Or that</b>

25
00:01:42.208 --> 00:01:46.083
<b>man is merely a mixture of</b>
<b>some substances and chemicals?</b>

26
00:01:46.083 --> 00:01:47.875
<b>Then why grieve?</b>

27
00:01:47.875 --> 00:01:51.583
<b>Do we become so overwhelmed with grief at</b>
<b>the destruction of physical elements?</b>

28
00:01:51.583 --> 00:01:53.541
<b>It never happens that</b>

29
00:01:53.541 --> 00:01:56.416
<b>when an earthen pot breaks,</b>

30
00:01:56.416 --> 00:02:02.375
<b>or the water in it is wasted, or when</b>
<b>a fire extinguishes, we sink into deep sorrow. </b>

31
00:02:02.375 --> 00:02:07.750
<b>Nor do we grieve when some substance or</b>
<b>chemical is wasted, do we?</b>

32
00:02:07.750 --> 00:02:08.708
<b>No right?</b>

33
00:02:08.708 --> 00:02:12.875
<b>then how can we grieve over the destruction of</b>
<b>human body made of physical elements?</b>

34
00:02:12.875 --> 00:02:14.916
<b>Understand it this way too</b>

35
00:02:14.916 --> 00:02:17.791
<b>what is destined to happen,</b>

36
00:02:17.791 --> 00:02:19.833
<b>how can there be grief over it?</b>

37
00:02:19.833 --> 00:02:24.250
<b>Will everyone's death be prevented if</b>
<b>Arjun doesn't fight?</b>

38
00:02:24.250 --> 00:02:25.375
<b>No, right?</b>

39
00:02:25.375 --> 00:02:27.916
<b>Then why grieve at the time of duty?</b>

40
00:02:27.916 --> 00:02:28.750
<b>Moreover,</b>

41
00:02:28.750 --> 00:02:30.625
<b>if Arjun doesn't fight,</b>

42
00:02:30.625 --> 00:02:34.666
<b>perhaps the Pandavas will be killed</b>
<b>in the Kauravas' attack,</b>

43
00:02:34.666 --> 00:02:39.875
<b>so even then, the death of loved ones is certain.</b>

44
00:02:39.875 --> 00:02:41.541
<b>It's as if Krishna is saying,</b>

45
00:02:41.541 --> 00:02:44.833
<b>Arjun, even if you look beyond</b>
<b>the soul's perspective,</b>

46
00:02:44.833 --> 00:02:48.291
<b>the body is still a puppet of physical elements,</b>

47
00:02:48.291 --> 00:02:49.791
<b>don't grieve for it.</b>

48
00:02:49.791 --> 00:02:51.958
<b>Whether you fight or not,</b>

49
00:02:51.958 --> 00:02:54.541
<b>death is certain,</b>

50
00:02:54.541 --> 00:02:57.541
<b>so why grieve over it?</b>

51
00:02:57.541 --> 00:03:01.916
<b>In any case, this is not a time for grief.</b>

52
00:03:02.625 --> 00:03:06.666


53
00:03:06.666 --> 00:03:08.958
<b>I know</b>

54
00:03:08.958 --> 00:03:16.166
<b>that right now, Arjun's mind harbors some</b>
<b>doubts about the soul's existence.</b>

55
00:03:16.166 --> 00:03:18.166
<b>This is natural,</b>

56
00:03:18.166 --> 00:03:23.125
<b>especially when one is distressed.</b>

57
00:03:23.125 --> 00:03:26.000
<b>This is why my effort here is to</b>

58
00:03:26.000 --> 00:03:31.666
<b>understand Arjun's doubt,</b>
<b>comprehend his distressed state,</b>

59
00:03:31.666 --> 00:03:38.250
<b>and explain to him from a</b>
<b>perspective he can relate to,</b>

60
00:03:38.250 --> 00:03:42.666
<b>that grief at this moment is futile.</b>

61
00:03:42.666 --> 00:03:47.125
<b>How do you react in such situations?</b>

62
00:03:47.125 --> 00:03:50.791
<b>When someone questions your logic?</b>

63
00:03:50.791 --> 00:03:54.958
<b>When they refuse to accept your perspective,</b>

64
00:03:54.958 --> 00:03:59.291
<b>or present an entirely opposite argument?</b>

65
00:03:59.291 --> 00:04:01.833
<b>Do you become agitated?</b>

66
00:04:01.833 --> 00:04:07.875
<b>Or do you present your</b>
<b>viewpoint with great patience?</b>

67
00:04:07.875 --> 00:04:12.000
<b>Here lies a significant signal,</b>

68
00:04:12.000 --> 00:04:14.416
<b>and a lesson too.</b>

69
00:04:14.416 --> 00:04:17.583
<b>If you quickly become agitated,</b>

70
00:04:17.583 --> 00:04:25.291
<b>it signals that perhaps you don't have</b>
<b>complete faith in your own perspective,</b>

71
00:04:25.291 --> 00:04:27.625
<b>because if you truly believe,</b>

72
00:04:27.625 --> 00:04:33.625
<b>then someone saying the opposite</b>
<b>won't make right wrong, will it?</b>

73
00:04:33.625 --> 00:04:37.000
<b>So why the anxiety?</b>

74
00:04:37.000 --> 00:04:41.625
<b>And this agitation also indicates</b>

75
00:04:41.625 --> 00:04:47.750
<b>that winning the argument has now</b>
<b>become more important than true knowledge.</b>

76
00:04:47.750 --> 00:04:53.458
<b>Because one who genuinely desires to</b>
<b>increase their knowledge</b>

77
00:04:53.458 --> 00:04:57.416
<b>listens patiently to opposing views,</b>

78
00:04:57.416 --> 00:05:05.416
<b>trying to see if there's something new to learn.</b>

79
00:05:05.416 --> 00:05:07.166
<b>Don't get agitated,</b>

80
00:05:07.166 --> 00:05:09.916
<b>listen to every perspective with patience,</b>

81
00:05:09.916 --> 00:05:13.875
<b>absorb what's worth learning</b>

82
00:05:13.875 --> 00:05:19.166
<b>then present your view calmly and patiently.</b>

83
00:05:19.166 --> 00:05:20.583
<b>After all,</b>

84
00:05:20.583 --> 00:05:26.333
<b>the purpose of debate is to reach the</b>
<b>right conclusion, isn't it?</b>

85
00:05:26.333 --> 00:05:28.416
<b>Who said what,</b>

86
00:05:28.416 --> 00:05:30.083
<b>how much they said</b>

87
00:05:30.083 --> 00:05:32.875
<b>where is that important?</b>

88
00:05:33.500 --> 00:05:37.166


89
00:05:37.166 --> 00:05:41.125
<b>Arjun has taken refuge in me.</b>

90
00:05:41.125 --> 00:05:43.000
<b>I know</b>

91
00:05:43.000 --> 00:05:48.000
<b>that fighting this war is right for him,</b>

92
00:05:48.000 --> 00:05:56.958
<b>and if I were to simply order him to fight without</b>
<b>any reasoning, without any explanation,</b>

93
00:05:56.958 --> 00:05:59.625
<b>he would never refuse.</b>

94
00:05:59.625 --> 00:06:00.958
<b>But</b>

95
00:06:00.958 --> 00:06:09.375
<b>then would he be able to show his full prowess</b>
<b>with complete capability?</b>

96
00:06:09.375 --> 00:06:11.166
<b>No.</b>

97
00:06:11.166 --> 00:06:12.500
<b>Moreover,</b>

98
00:06:12.500 --> 00:06:17.375
<b>the purpose here isn't just that</b>
<b>he follows my word,</b>

99
00:06:17.375 --> 00:06:23.500
<b>the purpose is also that he grasps and</b>
<b>embraces the right knowledge.</b>

100
00:06:23.500 --> 00:06:29.000
<b>Because this knowledge will help him</b>
<b>not just in this war, but throughout his life.</b>

101
00:06:29.000 --> 00:06:33.000
<b>The purpose here is solely Arjun's elevation.</b>

102
00:06:33.000 --> 00:06:34.166
<b>In family too,</b>

103
00:06:34.166 --> 00:06:39.708
<b>wouldn't you want the same for</b>
<b>your younger ones, for the coming generation</b>

104
00:06:39.708 --> 00:06:42.125
<b>that they become self-reliant,</b>

105
00:06:42.125 --> 00:06:47.041
<b>that whatever work they do, they do</b>
<b>with complete self-confidence?</b>

106
00:06:47.041 --> 00:06:51.250
<b>For this, it's essential that instead of</b>
<b>giving them strict orders</b>

107
00:06:51.250 --> 00:06:55.791
<b>or forcing them to follow your words,</b>

108
00:06:55.791 --> 00:06:58.083
<b>you give them the right perspective,</b>

109
00:06:58.083 --> 00:06:59.291
<b>right knowledge,</b>

110
00:06:59.291 --> 00:07:01.666
<b>suggest the right path.</b>

111
00:07:01.666 --> 00:07:05.916
<b>And inspire them to walk that path.</b>

112
00:07:05.916 --> 00:07:10.166
<b>Explain to them the reasoning</b>
<b>behind your suggestions,</b>

113
00:07:10.166 --> 00:07:14.375
<b>the logic behind your thoughts.</b>

114
00:07:14.375 --> 00:07:16.958
<b>This will lead to their progress,</b>

115
00:07:16.958 --> 00:07:19.666
<b>and increase their respect for you too.</b>

116
00:07:20.250 --> 00:07:24.083


117
00:07:24.083 --> 00:07:25.958
<b>Here is the effort</b>

118
00:07:25.958 --> 00:07:29.500
<b>to make Arjun understand</b>
<b>from every perspective.</b>

119
00:07:29.500 --> 00:07:33.875
<b>To show him that whichever way he looks,</b>

120
00:07:33.875 --> 00:07:37.208
<b>the conclusion to fight is indeed right.</b>

121
00:07:37.208 --> 00:07:42.541
<b>When Arjun weighs and</b>
<b>examines each perspective,</b>

122
00:07:42.541 --> 00:07:45.250
<b>all his illusions will dissolve,</b>

123
00:07:45.250 --> 00:07:48.333
<b>all doubts will vanish.</b>

124
00:07:48.333 --> 00:07:49.750
<b>And when this happens,</b>

125
00:07:49.750 --> 00:07:52.875
<b>his purpose will become crystal clear,</b>

126
00:07:52.875 --> 00:07:54.750
<b>he will have self-confidence,</b>

127
00:07:54.750 --> 00:08:00.125
<b>he will move swiftly towards achieving his goal.</b>

128
00:08:00.125 --> 00:08:04.625
<b>Isn't this the very foundation of success?</b>

129
00:08:04.625 --> 00:08:11.541
<b>A completely clear purpose, self-confidence,</b>
<b>and movement in the right direction.</b>

130
00:08:11.541 --> 00:08:16.166
<b>This will serve you well in professional life too.</b>

131
00:08:16.166 --> 00:08:18.125
<b>Don't rush.</b>

132
00:08:18.125 --> 00:08:24.291
<b>While making any plan, understand</b>
<b>your situation thoroughly,</b>

133
00:08:24.291 --> 00:08:29.250
<b>examine problems from different angles,</b>

134
00:08:29.250 --> 00:08:33.750
<b>clear all your doubts.</b>

135
00:08:33.750 --> 00:08:37.000
<b>After doing this, the plan that emerges</b>

136
00:08:37.000 --> 00:08:43.916
<b>will have both a clear purpose and</b>
<b>you'll be filled with confidence.Z</b>

137
00:08:43.916 --> 00:08:48.250
<b>In such case, the success of the plan is certain.</b>

